.\"
.\" SEMGET(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SEMGET 2 "June 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
semget \- get a System V semaphore set identifier
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sem.h>
.PP
.BI "int semget(key_t " key ", int " nsems ", int " semflg ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR semget ()
returns the identifier of the System V semaphore set associated with
.IR key .
A new set of
.I nsems
semaphores is created if
.I key
has the value
.B IPC_PRIVATE
or if no existing set is associated with
.I key
and
.B IPC_CREAT
is set in
.IR semflg .
.PP
The low 9 bits of
.I semflg
define the permissions of the set.  If
.B IPC_CREAT
and
.B IPC_EXCL
are both set then the call fails with
.B EEXIST
if a set already exists for
.IR key .
.PP
On creation
.I nsems
must be greater than 0 and not greater than
.BR SEMMSL .
For access to an existing set
.I nsems
may be 0 (don't care) or any value not larger than the set's size.
The semaphores in a newly created set are initialised to 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success the semaphore set identifier (a non-negative integer) is
returned.  On error \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
A set exists for
.I key
but the caller lacks permission.
.TP
.B EEXIST
.B IPC_CREAT
and
.B IPC_EXCL
were set and a set already exists for
.IR key .
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I nsems
is out of range for the requested operation.
.TP
.B ENOENT
No set exists for
.I key
and
.B IPC_CREAT
was not set.
.TP
.B ENOSPC
The system-wide limit on semaphore sets
.RB ( SEMMNI )
would be exceeded.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Insufficient memory to create the set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR semop (2),
.BR semctl (2),
.BR ftok (3)
